The cache uses a 64-pixel real-event context for optical-flow inference,
then crops back to the 320 x 480 target region. The videos use a shared
color scale across stages and 5x slower playback. These are visualization
examples of cached solver responses.

The spatial-compression baselines in nlidnet/models/baselines/temporal.py
adapt the ConvTran and InceptionTime implementations from NLID.
The RAW, ROI and event-representation preparation follows
create_6roi_dataset_from_raw.py, create_data.py and NLID preprocessing.
RGB appearance controls follow rgb_resnet34_single_frame_ablation.py and
rgb_resnet34_firstframe_diagnostics.py. Grad-CAM export and event overlays
follow export_gradcam_offline_cache_all.py and prepare_gradcam_data.py.

The UR5e program retains its DH-Robotics URCap source declarations.

